The escalation text, `too many failures (1/2): verification gates failed: elevation`, describes the verification-loop counter rather than the controlling persisted budget. ASG's `src/ai_strategy_generator/multistep/_arc_runner/runtime/run_arc_runner.py:4513` charges the two failed feedback builds; `:4828-4838` charges this verification failure against `max(3, max_failures)`. `pipeline/repair_budget.py:16-28` increments the same counter and stops at three. The state records three implementation repairs. This explains the stop without a budget or gate defect. Worker-side gate execution was prohibited by its role; not running local checks is not the cause. The one-line remedy is source-traced, **not runtime-verified** here.

